# bloc.rules — flutter_bloc mechanics (load only if ADR chose flutter_bloc)
# SOP: sop/bloc.md
# Guardrails: guardrails/state-management.md
# If project ADR chose Riverpod or another paradigm, skip this file; use state.rules + project rules.

## Files
MUST      BLOC-1  Layout: <x>_cubit/{x_cubit.dart, x_state.dart} or <x>_bloc/{x_bloc.dart, x_event.dart, x_state.dart}; state class name = owner stem + State.
MUST      BLOC-2  Class names XCubit / XBloc / XState / XEvent in files x_cubit.dart etc.

## Events
MUST      STATE-11 Declare `sealed class XEvent extends Equatable` with const constructors and props.
MUST      BLOC-3  Name events as facts or requests: LoginRequested, OtpSubmitted, ChatPinned. No `On` prefix, no `Event` suffix on subclasses.
MUST      STATE-10 Register an on<E> handler for every declared event; delete unused events.
MUST-NOT  STATE-10b Add public methods on a Bloc that emit directly; the Bloc API is add(event).

## Emit safety
MUST      STATE-5  Write `if (isClosed) return;` after every await and at the top of every stream/bus handler before emit.
MUST      BLOC-4   Guard re-entry: an in-flight guard covering loading, paginating and syncing as applicable at the start of fetch/submit methods.
MUST-NOT  STATE-16 Use Future.delayed in a Bloc/Cubit to wait for another component.

## Concurrency (no bloc_concurrency in project)
SHOULD    BLOC-5  Submit/create/delete: early-return while in flight (droppable). Search: debounce + ignore stale results by request id (restartable). Ordered mutations: sequential queue.
MAY       BLOC-6  Propose bloc_concurrency transformers via ADR when a Bloc genuinely needs per-event policies.

## Dependencies
MUST      DI-1    Constructor-inject abstractions (XRepository, connectivity monitor, event bus, session provider).
MUST-NOT  STATE-7 Resolve from the DI container ($LOOKUP, e.g. sl<>()) inside a Cubit/Bloc.
MUST-NOT  STATE-6 Import Flutter UI, hold BuildContext, navigate, toast, show loaders, or context.read another Bloc inside a Cubit/Bloc.

## Providing
MUST      BLOC-7  Provide screen state via BlocProvider(create: ...) at the route/screen composition root (PR-E1 router: e.g. AutoRouteWrapper.wrappedRoute, GoRoute builder).
MUST      BLOC-8  Use BlocProvider.value only to pass an existing instance into dialogs, sheets or nested routes.
MUST-NOT  DI-6    Register Cubits/Blocs as singletons; BlocProvider owns and closes factories.
MAY       BLOC-LOCAL-1   Construct dependency-free UI cubits directly in BlocProvider without DI registration.

## Consuming
SHOULD    STATE-15 BlocSelector or BlocBuilder+buildWhen for rendering; BlocListener+listenWhen for one-shot side effects; BlocConsumer when both; context.read<X>() for actions.
MUST      STATE-12 Keep navigation/toast/loader/dialog in listeners only.

## Cross-Bloc
MUST      STATE-8  Subscribe to typed bus events in the constructor through the app's established subscription helper or owned StreamSubscription; never inject or read another Bloc.
MUST      STATE-9  close(): cancel debounce keys, await disposeSubscriptions(), cancel stream subs, then super.close().

## Debounce
MUST      BLOC-LOCAL-2 Use the selected debounce approach with per-instance ownership and cancel it in close(); a Timer or established stream transformer is sufficient. Do not add EasyDebounce unless already chosen.

## Testing
MUST      TEST-1  Ship state-holder tests for success, failure, no-internet (if applicable), pagination stop, and dispose/closed safety where relevant. Use the test stack in docs/project/flutter/project-rules.md.

## Project
PROJECT   See docs/project/flutter/project-rules.md for overrides and open decisions.
MUST-NOT  Invent class/file names from profiles/reference/ or example ADRs when docs/project/flutter/ still has _TBD_ stubs.
